# Working-tree line endings are normalized to LF everywhere.
#
# Why this file exists: `core.autocrlf=true` is set on the Windows clones this repository is
# developed on, and with no rules to override it, git checked every text file out as CRLF.
# That is invisible until a test reads source and searches for a literal "\n". It already
# happened: `tests/task-assignee-identity.test.mjs` searches `src/main.js` for '\n}\n', which
# cannot occur in CRLF text, so five of its tests failed on every Windows checkout and passed
# on CI. See .ai/known-issues.md.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text by content and normalize it; `eol=lf` then fixes the working
# tree to LF on every platform. The explicit extension list below makes the text files certain
# rather than detected, because a file git guesses wrong about stays wrong silently.
#
# Note for future source-scanning tests: normalizing the WORKING TREE is not a substitute for
# normalizing on READ. Still write `readFileSync(...).replace(/\r\n/g, '\n')`, as the other
# source-scanning tests do, so a test cannot be broken by a checkout configuration.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Text, stated rather than detected.
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.webmanifest text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Binary. Never normalized, never diffed as text, never line-ending converted. These must be
# listed explicitly: `text=auto` alone is a content guess, and a misjudged binary becomes a
# corrupted file rather than a failed check.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.apk   binary
*.zip   binary

# Windows batch files. LF works, but CRLF is what every other .bat on the machine has and what
# cmd.exe was built around; leave them alone.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
